          columnar object 
          of all the entries present in the opticsIMDs3pPITTPTable."
::= { opticsIMTrsCommonMibObject 17 }


opticsIMAllDs3PathParityViolationMonitoringRemoving OBJECT-TYPE
     SYNTAX				OpticsIMDs3ParityViolationMonitoringRemoving
     MAX-ACCESS		read-write 
     STATUS				current
     DESCRIPTION
        " This object is used to specify, in one shot, whether the Parity Violation Monitoring Removing
         (PVMR) is enabled on path  direction on all the ds3 lines. As consequence of a set operation 
          on this object,  the agent has to set to the required value the ParityViolationMonitoringRemoving columnar object 
          of all the entries present in the opticsIMDs3PathTTPTable."
::= { opticsIMTrsCommonMibObject 18 }


opticsIMAllDs3AISSignalType OBJECT-TYPE
     SYNTAX				OpticsIMDs3AISSignalType
     MAX-ACCESS		read-write 
     STATUS				current
     DESCRIPTION
        " This object is used to specify, in one shot, the type of AIS signal to be inserted (if enabled) 
        on all the ds3 lines. As consequence of a set operation on this object,  the agent has to set to the
        required value the AISSignalType columnar object of all the entries present in the
        opticsIMDs3pPITTPTable."
::= { opticsIMTrsCommonMibObject 19 }


opticsIMAllDs3pPIAISInsertion OBJECT-TYPE
     SYNTAX				OpticsIMAISInsertion
     MAX-ACCESS		read-write 
     STATUS				current
     DESCRIPTION
        " This object is used to specify, in one shot, whether the AIS (Alarm Indication Signal) insertion
         is allowed on pPI direction on all the ds3 lines. As consequence of a set operation 
          on this object,  the agent has to set to the required value the AISInsertion columnar object 
          of all the entries present in the opticsIMDs3pPITTPTable."
::= { opticsIMTrsCommonMibObject 20 }



opticsIMAllDs3PathAISInsertion OBJECT-TYPE
     SYNTAX				OpticsIMAISInsertion
     MAX-ACCESS		read-write 
     STATUS				current
     DESCRIPTION
        " This object is used to specify, in one shot, whether the AIS (Alarm Indication Signal) insertion
         is allowed on path direction on all the ds3 lines. As consequence of a set operation on this object,
         the agent has to set to the required value the AISInsertion columnar object of all the entries present 
         in the opticsIMDs3PathTTPTable."
::= { opticsIMTrsCommonMibObject 21 }


opticsIMAllDs3AISSignalTiming OBJECT-TYPE
     SYNTAX				OpticsIMDs3AISSignalTiming
     MAX-ACCESS		read-write 
     STATUS				current
     DESCRIPTION
        " This object is used to specify, in one shot, the timing for AIS signal on all the ds3 lines. As
         consequence of a set operation on this object,  the agent has to set to the required value the
